# ── TUNING: the knobs, and where they come from ─────────────────────────────
#
# These used to live ONLY in the unit's Environment= lines, which meant two bad
# things. Changing one needed an SSH session and a daemon-reload, so the owner
# could not; and running the script by hand gave a DIFFERENT PROGRAM, because a
# bare run inherits none of them. That second failure has cost this project a
# day already (CLAUDE.md 7.14, the wrap-desk floor that defaulted to 0 and paged
# the owner with a false 50,000 PCN alert).
#
# So the order of precedence is now, highest first:
#
#   1. TUNING_FILE   -- JSON, written by the admin panel. The owner's control.
#   2. Environment=  -- the unit file. Still honoured, as the fallback.
#   3. the defaults below.
#
# and EVERY run prints which source each value came from. A bot that spends
# money must say what it is running with; inferring it from a config file
# somebody believes they deployed is how this goes wrong.
#
# A tuning file that is PRESENT but unreadable, unparsable, or carries a value
# outside its bounds is FATAL: the keeper refuses to trade and alerts. It does
# not fall back. An unknown setting is unknown, never a default -- that is the
# project's oldest rule (CLAUDE.md 7.1) and it matters most on the one process
# here that can move money on its own.
#
# The bounds are enforced HERE as well as in the panel. A check only the writer
# performs is not a check (CLAUDE.md 7.12).
